WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.211
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.511 --> 00:00:08.735
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.035 --> 00:00:15.704
Unit eleven: Sustainability. Today you will say what is necessary with 'need to be' + past participle.

4
00:00:16.004 --> 00:00:18.784
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:23.338
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:25.568
Circular economy.

7
00:00:26.583 --> 00:00:30.777
Circular economy means a system where things are reused, not thrown away.

8
00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:34.811
In a circular economy, old phones become new ones.

9
00:00:35.417 --> 00:00:38.499
Your turn. Say: Circular economy.

10
00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:42.741
Circular economy.

11
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:44.995
Renewable resource.

12
00:00:45.983 --> 00:00:49.399
Renewable resource means a resource that nature replaces.

13
00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:52.053
Sunlight is a renewable resource.

14
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.964
Your turn. Say: Renewable resource.

15
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.556
Renewable resource.

16
00:01:01.317 --> 00:01:03.119
Environmental stewardship.

17
00:01:04.117 --> 00:01:08.102
Environmental stewardship means taking care of nature responsibly.

18
00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:11.610
Planting trees is environmental stewardship.

19
00:01:12.217 --> 00:01:16.018
Your turn. Say: Environmental stewardship.

20
00:01:18.867 --> 00:01:21.319
Environmental stewardship.

21
00:01:22.083 --> 00:01:23.560
Carbon neutrality.

22
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:28.012
Carbon neutrality means adding no extra carbon to the air.

23
00:01:28.617 --> 00:01:31.998
The company aims for carbon neutrality by 2040.

24
00:01:32.583 --> 00:01:35.793
Your turn. Say: Carbon neutrality.

25
00:01:38.633 --> 00:01:40.505
Carbon neutrality.

26
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.460
Biodegradable.

27
00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.251
Biodegradable means able to break down naturally.

28
00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:49.511
Banana-leaf packaging is biodegradable.

29
00:01:50.117 --> 00:01:52.966
Your turn. Say: Biodegradable.

30
00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.103
Biodegradable.

31
00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.432
Sustainable development.

32
00:02:00.417 --> 00:02:04.007
Sustainable development means growth that does not harm the future.

33
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:07.220
Sustainable development protects our rivers.

34
00:02:07.817 --> 00:02:10.666
Your turn. Say: Sustainable development.

35
00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.116
Sustainable development.

36
00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:17.107
Green innovation.

37
00:02:18.117 --> 00:02:21.649
Green innovation means new ideas that help the environment.

38
00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:24.702
Solar boats are a green innovation.

39
00:02:25.317 --> 00:02:28.793
Your turn. Say: Green innovation.

40
00:02:31.633 --> 00:02:33.076
Green innovation.

41
00:02:33.817 --> 00:02:35.154
Conservation effort.

42
00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.893
Conservation effort means work to protect nature.

43
00:02:39.483 --> 00:02:42.284
Conservation efforts saved the Mekong dolphins.

44
00:02:42.883 --> 00:02:46.128
Your turn. Say: Conservation effort.

45
00:02:48.967 --> 00:02:50.548
Conservation effort.

46
00:02:51.283 --> 00:02:53.062
Ecological balance.

47
00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:57.106
Ecological balance means nature working in harmony.

48
00:02:57.717 --> 00:03:00.250
Cutting forests harms ecological balance.

49
00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:03.874
Your turn. Say: Ecological balance.

50
00:03:06.733 --> 00:03:08.408
Ecological balance.

51
00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:10.488
Resource management.

52
00:03:11.483 --> 00:03:14.377
Resource management means using resources carefully.

53
00:03:14.983 --> 00:03:17.679
Good resource management saves water.

54
00:03:18.283 --> 00:03:21.330
Your turn. Say: Resource management.

55
00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:25.795
Resource management.

56
00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:28.062
Long-term impact.

57
00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:32.652
Long-term impact means an effect that lasts many years.

58
00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:36.469
Plastic has a long-term impact on the sea.

59
00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:40.827
Your turn. Say: Long-term impact.

60
00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:45.910
Long-term impact.

61
00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.057
Climate resilience.

62
00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:52.524
Climate resilience means the ability to cope with climate change.

63
00:03:53.117 --> 00:03:55.673
Strong dams build climate resilience.

64
00:03:56.283 --> 00:03:59.330
Your turn. Say: Climate resilience.

65
00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:03.621
Climate resilience.

66
00:04:04.433 --> 00:04:08.281
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:04:09.117 --> 00:04:11.488
Visal, what does sustainability mean?

68
00:04:12.583 --> 00:04:17.009
It means resources need to be managed carefully for a sustainable future.

69
00:04:18.117 --> 00:04:19.977
What needs to be changed first?

70
00:04:21.083 --> 00:04:24.964
Plastic bags need to be replaced with biodegradable ones.

71
00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.248
And energy?

72
00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:32.764
Renewable resources like solar power need to be used more.

73
00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.621
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:36.483 --> 00:04:39.644
Grammar focus: Passive with need to be.

75
00:04:39.944 --> 00:04:41.177
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:41.883 --> 00:04:44.382
Resources need to be managed carefully.

77
00:04:45.283 --> 00:04:47.144
Plastic needs to be reduced.

78
00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.817
Forests need to be protected.

79
00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:58.864
Use 'need to be' + past participle to say something is necessary when the doer is not important. Use 'needs' with singular subjects.

80
00:04:59.617 --> 00:05:03.523
Be careful! Don't say: Resources need to managed carefully.

81
00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:09.010
Say: Resources need to be managed carefully.

82
00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:11.670
Say 'need to be' + past participle.

83
00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:15.560
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:17.554
Living for Tomorrow.

85
00:05:17.854 --> 00:05:21.409
Sustainability means meeting our needs without harming the future.

86
00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.852
Resources need to be managed carefully.

87
00:05:25.867 --> 00:05:28.992
Waste needs to be reduced through a circular economy.

88
00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.693
Green innovation and conservation efforts protect ecological balance.

89
00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.559
Every small action has a long-term impact.

90
00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:43.924
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:44.783 --> 00:05:46.330
Forests need to be blank.

92
00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:50.400
A, protected. B, protect. C, protecting.

93
00:05:53.933 --> 00:05:56.293
The answer is A: protected.

94
00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:59.937
Able to break down naturally means blank.

95
00:06:00.237 --> 00:06:04.425
A, biodegradable. B, renewable. C, circular.

96
00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:10.605
The answer is A: biodegradable.

97
00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:14.957
A resource that nature replaces is a blank resource.

98
00:06:15.257 --> 00:06:18.864
A, renewable. B, neutral. C, green.

99
00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.237
The answer is A: renewable.

100
00:06:25.433 --> 00:06:28.747
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:29.583 --> 00:06:32.233
What does sustainability mean to you personally?

102
00:06:41.017 --> 00:06:42.610
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:53.712
To me, sustainability means using only what I need. Plastic needs to be reduced, so I carry my own bottle and bag every day.

104
00:06:54.012 --> 00:06:55.698
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:56.583 --> 00:07:01.000
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and passive with need to be.

106
00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:06.019
Today's value is sustainable living. Buy less, reuse more, and protect our planet.

107
00:07:06.319 --> 00:07:08.856
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

108
00:07:09.156 --> 00:07:12.539
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

